  "notes": {
    "revision": "PWNAGE-47000/v0.7.5-beta: registry_version 9 adds the three GUI Tri-Link remote-access entries (XRDP, VNC, scrcpy). The three Serial/Wi-Fi/USB SSH console entries are preserved unchanged.",
    "tree_apps_states": "complete | in_progress | shared-assets-not-an-app (the dir MUST exist) | planned (must NOT exist yet; DEFER until it lands). Enforced by tools/s10plus/a33/verify-app-registry.py - a dangling directory in a present-state entry is a FAILED verdict, never a warning.",
    "required_apps_not_yet_in_tree": "Concept-level inventory of mission-required apps with no tree directory yet. Each entry names the owning build group and its ledger briq; the verifier fails if that briq file does not exist in docs/beta-finalization/workqueue/ or if the briq's component does not match owner_group.",
    "registry_version_6_tri_link": "NUXEL-28000 registers three distinct console entries in apps[] and apps.js; the registry revision is 6 so launcher/native/HTTP consumers cannot drift silently.",
    "registry_version_9_gui_tri_link": "org.nuxel.RemoteDesktopXRDP (separate X11 RDP/TLS session), org.nuxel.RemoteDesktopVNC (active Phoc Wayland screen sharing) and org.nuxel.ScrcpyMirror (Android ADB only) are distinct from the serial/SSH console entries and use the separate system.remote-desktop Bridge namespace."
  }
